vendored 2026-10-08: src/befaco/ = the originals, with seven small changes (upstream-changes.diff):
  Commons.h      the two ARMv8 assembler lines (vmaxnm / vminnm) can be switched off: -DONEIROI_PORTABLE_MINMAX (the MPC is ARMv7)
  Echo.h         the taps are recalculated when an external clock's period changes, not only when DENSITY moves
  DelayLine.h    a read outside the buffer wraps inside it (resonator and ambience delays pushed out of range by modulation)
  LooperBuffer.h the read position is wrapped into the buffer before it is converted to an integer
added 2026-10-26 (memory leaks: the module never unloads its patch, a plugin does with every removal from a track):
  LooperBuffer.h the destructor frees the looper's 2 MB buffer
  Modulation.h   the seven LFO shapes are kept and freed with the modulator (MorphingOscillator does not own them)
  Oneiroi.h      the destructor frees the input and output DC filters
Ui.h, ParamController.h, Led.h, Midi.h and the patch class are kept for reference and not compiled: mpc/oneiroi_engine.cc
stands in for them.
src/owl/ = the parts of Rebel Technology's OWL library the patch is written against, unchanged:
https://github.com/pingdynasty/OwlProgram commit 3942f8294df79f0456e41264cfa734645ba4fe90 (LibSource/, Source/; GPL-3.0-or-later, src/owl/LICENSE).
mpc/ = the MPC engine (new, GPL-3.0-or-later): oneiroi_engine.cc; mi_engine.h (dev-tools/mi, MIT); engine.h (the framework's).
